      "content": "that's a fair point, but it feels like pretty much every time a government says they're doing it for \"stability\" or \"national security,\" it's just a cover for silencing critics or stopping protests. isn't it more accurate to say that most legitimate security concerns can be handled without pulling the plug on the whole internet?",
